  "raw": "ima Vavi\nIn July there was confusion among the membership of Unions’ Coordinating Council (UCC) over what form trade union federation Cosatu should take, some affiliate formations were demanding the formation of the formation of an alliance with other progressive organisations such as the Congress of South African Trade Unions (Cosatu). Now finally Ministers of Public Enterprises and the Department of Public Service and Administration have addressed workers and employers on national developments under President Cyril Ramaphosa. Political analyst and associate professor at Wits Economic Education Institute Ralph Mathekga believes this has been nailed down as the formation of a new federation based on the model of SA-EU Free Trade Area will unite sovereign states. Newly appointed Finance Minister, Malusi Gigaba gave the all clear that no enterprise level restructuring would be contemplated or implemented for the first five years of Public Enterprises being led by French consulting firm Deloitte. He continued saying excluding America’s recent economic turmoil from South Africa’s",
